  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Bombay potatoes are par-cooked potato cubes fried in spiced oil with mustard seeds, "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "curry leaves",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "curry-leaves"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ", and a quick tomato sauce. The par-cooking step keeps the inside fluffy while the outside crisps in the pan. They need a hot pan and patience: do not move the potatoes too often, or they will steam rather than fry."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
